dispatch({ type: "submit" });`),iq("useMemo — what does it cache and when is it worth it?","useMemo(fn, deps) runs fn during render and caches its return value, recomputing only when a dependency changes. Use it for genuinely expensive calculations, or to keep a referential identity stable (an object/array passed to a memoized child or used as another hook's dependency). It is not free: React stores the value and compares deps every render, so wrapping trivial math is noise. With the React Compiler enabled, most of this memoization is inserted automatically and you write far less useMemo by hand.",`// expensive derived data — recompute only when inputs change
